  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Water Scarcity Initiative Program for the MENA-Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Water Scarcity Initiative (WSI) is a regional partnership platform, coordinated by the Regional FAO Office for the Near East and North Africa (FAO RNE). This program that contributes to the implementation of the WSI platform is implemented by six partner organizations: FAO-RNE (contract party), UNESCWA, UNICEF, IWMI, ICARDA and ICBA (Dubai-based).

The program aims to strengthen a knowledge and evidence-based response for participating countries to address water scarcity and sustainable food production, in a context of climate change. This is a pioneering program, with a strong focus on the integration of water and food by evidence-based policy dialogue. The program is aimed at the most prominent challenge of the region: water scarcity.</narrative>
  </description>
